# Aegis safety

Paper trading is the default. Live trading stays disabled until the owner explicitly approves it.

## Live gates

Live order submission requires all of:

- `AEGIS_TRADING_MODE=live`
- `AEGIS_LIVE_ARMED=true`
- `AEGIS_KILL_SWITCH=false`

Do not weaken startup validation in `src/aegis/config/settings.py` or gates in `src/aegis/guards/live.py`. Models must never write these flags.

## Credential plane

Toobit API secrets may exist only in the exchange adapter / secret injection path. Analysts, Jev, and the LLM Supervisor must never receive exchange credentials, signing material, or execution tools.

Never call `POST /api/v1/account/withdraw` or any withdrawal endpoint.

## Honest external integrations

Do not invent Toobit or TypeSafe Jev endpoints, fields, or behaviors. Prefer verified facts in `docs/API_CONTRACTS.md`. Unverified behavior stays behind an interface and is documented in the module `LIMITATIONS.md`.

Do not invent numeric risk-policy values (leverage, size, loss, drawdown). See `docs/RISK_POLICY.md` — unapproved parameters block live enforcement.

## Forbidden patterns

- LangGraph or similar agent tool loops that can grant models execution tools (ADR 0002)
- Toobit Agent Trade Kit or other AI-facing order bridges (ADR 0007)
- Blind retry of timed-out or HTTP 5xx order submits (reconcile first)
- Mixing paper and live ledgers
- Reading or printing secrets from `.env`, `.env.local`, private keys, or credential files (use `.env.example` only)

## Authority

The deterministic Risk Engine is the only authority that may APPROVE a new trade. Prefer `NO_TRADE` / REJECT when critical evidence or state is missing, stale, or inconsistent.
